EPIC-260715-21g2pi_product-experience-and-security/STORY-260715-n5dt84_onboarding-accessibility-and-migration/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-21g2pi_product-experience-and-security/STORY-260715-n5dt84_onboarding-accessibility-and-migration/README.md:10:1. A first-time user on iOS and macOS can understand the self-hosted SSH model, complete or resume prerequisites, create a profile, trust a host, acknowledge privacy terms, grant VPN permission, connect, understand capability or failure, obtain help, and disconnect. 2. Privacy disclosure appears before the first enable action and onboarding does not claim anonymity, a Relux exit network, or capabilities not present in the selected mode. 3. All M4 surfaces have stable shared accessibility identifiers, meaningful labels/hints/values, logical focus, keyboard operation on macOS, VoiceOver operation, supported text scaling, sufficient contrast, and reduced-motion behavior. 4. User-facing strings are externalized, pseudo-localization and text expansion pass, and the approved launch-locale policy and fallback are documented. 5. A reviewed decision selects legacy SOCKS coexistence, replacement, or retirement and defines handling of host/account/port defaults, existing release history, bundle/storage identity, rollback, and user messaging before migration code runs. 6. Automated UI journeys plus named physical Apple-silicon Mac acceptance, with the iPhone journey deferred with iOS under ADR-024, cover first run, relaunch/resume, permission denial, empty/error recovery, migration path, full/degraded/failure states, diagnostics, accessibility, and screenshot review.
EPIC-260715-21g2pi_product-experience-and-security/STORY-260715-n5dt84_onboarding-accessibility-and-migration/TASK-260715-1fk4ja_add-onboarding-migration-localization-and-accessibility-ui-tests/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-21g2pi_product-experience-and-security/STORY-260715-n5dt84_onboarding-accessibility-and-migration/TASK-260715-1fk4ja_add-onboarding-migration-localization-and-accessibility-ui-tests/README.md:10:1. Page Objects cover every onboarding state/transition and approved migration branch on macOS, with the iOS rows deferred under ADR-024, with deterministic fixtures, typed launch arguments, conditional waits, and no sleeps. 2. Tests prove privacy acknowledgement precedes first enable, permission and feature handoffs resume correctly, migration is explicit/idempotent/recoverable, and no safety gate is bypassed. 3. Locale/pseudo/expansion rows detect missing/stale keys, placeholder errors, clipping, misplaced fingerprint/technical text, privacy-copy mismatch, and required RTL defects. 4. VoiceOver and keyboard journeys complete the primary product flow on macOS; focus, roles, values, errors, announcements, scaling, contrast, motion, and secure-field privacy pass. 5. Extracted screenshots/snapshot diffs are visually reviewed and the TASK-ID-scoped outcome records environments, commands, xcresults, migration fixtures, locale/accessibility matrix, and redacted evidence.
EPIC-260715-21g2pi_product-experience-and-security/STORY-260715-n5dt84_onboarding-accessibility-and-migration/TASK-260715-2unyf6_implement-m4-accessibility-semantics-focus-and-motion/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-21g2pi_product-experience-and-security/STORY-260715-n5dt84_onboarding-accessibility-and-migration/TASK-260715-2unyf6_implement-m4-accessibility-semantics-focus-and-motion/README.md:10:1. An accessibility inventory maps every interactive/status/error element to a meaningful role, label, value, hint, group, identifier, focus behavior, and platform keyboard action where applicable. 2. VoiceOver can complete configure, key action, trust/cancel, connect/degraded/failure, diagnostics/export/delete, privacy, onboarding, migration, and disconnect journeys without inaccessible gestures or secret-value exposure. 3. macOS journeys are fully keyboard operable with deterministic focus/modal return and no pointer-only or status-item-only action. 4. Supported text scaling/Dynamic Type, long localization, contrast, color-independent meaning, reduced motion, and reduced-transparency behavior avoid clipping, overlap, lost controls, and unsafe animation dependence. 5. Automated checks plus manual Accessibility Inspector/VoiceOver/keyboard evidence on the named Apple-silicon Mac, with the iPhone row deferred under ADR-024, record issues, fixes, screenshots, and pass/fail by surface.
