EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2xnj3v_apple-capability-provisioning/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2xnj3v_apple-capability-provisioning/README.md:10:1. Evidence confirms Relux Works organization enrollment, team identifier, responsible roles, registered physical devices, and access to manage identifiers, capabilities, certificates, and profiles. 2. A reviewed identity matrix defines unique iOS and macOS host and extension bundle IDs plus the minimum App Group and Keychain groups. 3. Host and extension App IDs and development profiles contain the exact required packet-tunnel, App Group, and Keychain entitlements with no unrelated capability. 4. A disposable provider is installed through its containing app, saves a NETunnelProviderManager configuration, launches, reports a versioned probe result, and stops cleanly on one named Apple-silicon Mac; the physical-iPhone row is a named deferred gap under ADR-024. 5. Exported entitlement and profile inspections match the planned matrix and contain no secret material. 6. A Gate P0 record includes device and OS versions, Xcode and source revisions, bundle/profile identifiers, commands or steps, observed results, failures, and an explicit pass or fail verdict.
