EPIC-260715-3810we_tcp-dns-system-vpn/STORY-260715-eto58m_vpn-manager-and-extension-lifecycle/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-3810we_tcp-dns-system-vpn/STORY-260715-eto58m_vpn-manager-and-extension-lifecycle/README.md:10:1. Each platform creates or updates only the Relux-owned manager configuration and does not duplicate or overwrite unrelated VPN configurations. 2. The thin providers delegate live work to ReluxTunnelCore, report versioned state, and stop promptly with all owned work cancelled. 3. Forwarding and truthful system VPN state continue while the containing app is suspended or terminated. 4. Automated lifecycle tests cover persistence, start cancellation, provider failures, messages, stop reasons, stale configuration, and repeated cycles. 5. Physical Apple-silicon Mac evidence proves, with the iPhone row deferred under ADR-024, approved host verification and auth, dual-stack representative TCP, leak-free DNS, exit-host external IP, no route loop, host-app independence, disconnect, and cleanup.
